  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional Health Collaboration Project with Ukraine</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Goal: Capacity of the Ukraine&apos;s health authorities in physical rehabilitation, mental health, antibiotic stewardship and infection prevention and control sustained.

The project has three main outcomes: 
1. Administrative capacity of Ukraine&apos;s health authorities in monitoring, use of data for policy, and resource allocation with a focus on AMR-IPC, rehabilitation and mental health is sustained. 
2. Quality of rehabilitation services in selected sites improved.  
3. Access to crisis management, bereavement support and suicide prevention in selected sites increased.  

All outcomes have a set of pertaining outputs and project aims to reach the following five main target groups:  
a. technical staff of the national health authorities, including Ministry of Health, the Public Health Centre of Ukraine, and the National Health Service of Ukraine, 
b. healthcare workers,  
c. facility managers,  
d. students in relevant disciplines, and  
e. university teachers 

Norwegian partners include: Akershus University Hospital (Ahus grief unit and Ahus suicide unit), Regional Resource Center on Violence, Traumatic Stress, and Suicide Prevention, Eastern Region (RVTS &#xD8;st), and Sunnaas Rehabilitation Hospital</narrative>
  </description>
